# git-mutate, in Python. Behaviourally identical to the bash implementation: same CLI, same
# TOML schema, same output strings, same exit statuses. The bash version grew a data model it
# had nowhere to put -- a ten-field per-mutation record emulated in sidecar files, and ~60
# awk/sed/grep calls doing work a language with values does natively. This is that same tool
# with the record as a dataclass and the pipelines as expressions.
#
# What did NOT change, on purpose: every guard, the order of the report, the wording of every
# line, and the exit statuses. The test suite is the specification.

